## 4. Database Schema & Entities

The PostgreSQL schema is managed by Hibernate in the Spring backend and mapped via `prisma/schema.prisma` in the Express backend.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USER ||--o{ ORDER : "places"
    ORDER ||--|{ ORDER_ITEM : "contains"
    ORDER ||--o| PAYMENT : "has"
    MENU_ITEM ||--o{ ORDER_ITEM : "ordered in"
    MENU_ITEM }|--|{ ADDON : "supports"
    ORDER_ITEM }|--|{ ADDON : "includes"
    COUPON
    CAROUSEL_IMAGE

    USER {
        int id PK
        string name
        string email UK
        string phone
        string password
        string_array address
        string role "USER or ADMIN"
    }

    MENU_ITEM {
        int id PK
        string category
        string name
        string description
        float price
        boolean veg
        string imageUrl
    }

    ADDON {
        int id PK
        string category
        string name
        float price
    }

    ORDER {
        int id PK
        int userId FK "nullable"
        string customerName
        string customerEmail
        string customerPhone
        string deliveryAddress
        float totalAmount
        string status
        datetime createdAt
    }

    ORDER_ITEM {
        int id PK
        int orderId FK
        int menuItemId FK
        int quantity
    }

    PAYMENT {
        int id PK
        int orderId FK UK
        string razorpayOrderId
        string razorpayPaymentId
        string razorpaySignature
        string status
        datetime createdAt
        datetime updatedAt
    }

    COUPON {
        int id PK
        string code UK
        string discountType "FLAT or PERCENTAGE"
        float discountValue
        float minOrderValue
        datetime validUntil
        boolean active
    }

    CAROUSEL_IMAGE {
        int id PK
        string imageUrl
        boolean active
        int order
    }
```

### Table & Column Details:
- **`users` (`User`):**
  - Table name: `users` (avoiding SQL keyword collisions).
  - Passwords hashed with BCrypt.
  - Role defaults to `"USER"`. Accounts registered with email `admin@hungrylabs.com` automatically receive `"ADMIN"`.
  - `@JsonIgnore` on password and order relations to prevent serialization and circular loops.
- **`menu_item` (`MenuItem`):**
  - Stores food item definitions, categories (e.g. `Sandwiches`, `Burgers`, `Fries`, `Beverages`), `price`, and vegetarian flag.
  - Column `description` mapped to `desc` in Java entity (avoiding SQL `DESC` reserved keyword).
  - Many-to-Many join table with `Addon`: `menu_items_addons`.
- **`addon` (`Addon`):**
  - Reusable extras (e.g. Extra Cheese, Dip, Jalapeños) with specific prices.
- **`orders` (`Order`):**
  - Table name: `orders` (avoiding SQL `ORDER BY` reserved keyword).
  - Statuses: `PAYMENT PENDING` / `PENDING` -> `CONFIRMED` -> `PREPARING` -> `OUT_FOR_DELIVERY` -> `DELIVERED` (or `CANCELLED`, `FAILED`).
  - Contains full customer delivery details for non-registered or guest orders.
- **`OrderItem`:**
  - Connects `Order` and `MenuItem` with specific `quantity`.
  - Many-to-Many join table with `Addon`: `order_items_addons`.
- **`Payment`:**
  - One-to-One relation with `Order`.
  - Maps internal `orderId` to Razorpay's `razorpayOrderId` and transaction `razorpayPaymentId`.
- **`Coupon`:**
  - Unique promo `code` (e.g., `HUNGRY10`, `WELCOME50`).
  - `discountType`: `"FLAT"` (deducts exact ₹ amount) or `"PERCENTAGE"` (deducts % value).
  - `minOrderValue`: Minimum cart subtotal required to apply.

